WEBVTT

00:07.300 --> 00:08.969
What a run-down town.

00:08.970 --> 00:10.940
Is it really here?

00:11.410 --> 00:13.639
Yes, without a doubt.

00:13.640 --> 00:17.080
Soon the preparations for
the seal will be complete.

00:20.880 --> 00:22.750
Then let us get started.

00:23.850 --> 00:26.190
All the world bows to the Evening Star.

00:26.490 --> 00:28.650
And that which must be done is done.

00:30.190 --> 00:35.499
Hey who are you thinking of now?

00:35.500 --> 00:43.410
I am thinking of you

00:46.040 --> 00:48.709
I felt it when I opened my window

00:48.710 --> 00:50.949
Ah the smell of the night

00:50.950 --> 00:53.549
Whose face did I just see

00:53.550 --> 00:55.849
In my heart?

00:55.850 --> 00:58.589
When I was

00:58.590 --> 01:00.859
Soaked by the cold rain

01:00.860 --> 01:02.519
You were the only one

01:02.520 --> 01:05.459
To reach out your hand

01:05.460 --> 01:10.329
Why are you always

01:10.330 --> 01:14.939
The one to support me

01:14.940 --> 01:17.869
Each time

01:17.870 --> 01:22.139
I fall deeper in love

01:22.140 --> 01:27.379
Hey no matter what I do I want to see you

01:27.380 --> 01:32.089
Falling in love hurts

01:32.090 --> 01:34.819
You are always the only reason

01:34.820 --> 01:37.389
I feel happiness and heartache

01:37.390 --> 01:45.270
I am thinking of you

01:48.170 --> 01:56.170
Hey I want to see you

02:09.420 --> 02:10.785
Determined

02:09.420 --> 02:10.829
Step

02:10.786 --> 02:12.150
First

02:10.830 --> 02:12.130
It's just a dream.

02:13.900 --> 02:16.129
Good morning.
I'm all right.

02:16.130 --> 02:18.600
I just had a strange dream.

02:20.440 --> 02:21.899
<i>Now that I think about it,</i>

02:21.900 --> 02:24.900
<i>I feel like I had the same
dream when I came here.</i>

02:25.370 --> 02:29.370
<i>Could this have something to
do with the Tamayori princess?</i>

02:30.180 --> 02:32.410
I'll go ask Grandma.

02:37.520 --> 02:39.320
Good morning, Mitsuru.

02:39.590 --> 02:41.490
Good morning, Lady Tamaki.

02:42.660 --> 02:44.789
That looks delicious!

02:44.790 --> 02:47.029
Mitsuru, you're an amazing cook.

02:47.030 --> 02:48.960
Yesterday's was scrumptious, as well.

02:49.230 --> 02:51.030
Thank you very much.

02:51.430 --> 02:52.669
Have you seen Grandma?

02:52.670 --> 02:56.260
Lady Baba isn't seeing
anyone at the moment.

02:57.210 --> 02:58.470
Why?

02:59.310 --> 03:00.339
Who can say?

03:00.340 --> 03:02.170
That's what I was told.

03:07.350 --> 03:10.280
I wonder why Grandma isn't seeing anyone.

03:10.720 --> 03:12.690
Good morning, everybody.

03:14.320 --> 03:18.190
Ah, so you're the transfer
student, Kasuga, right?

03:19.060 --> 03:20.529
I'm Fiona Ashiuma.

03:20.530 --> 03:21.530
Nice to meet you.

03:22.060 --> 03:23.330
It's nice to meet you.

03:23.730 --> 03:24.760
Okay!

03:25.000 --> 03:26.490
Then let's start class.

03:27.140 --> 03:28.870
Today is listening.

03:29.270 --> 03:32.669
So that teacher started
here three months ago,

03:32.670 --> 03:35.700
and on top of being
gorgeous, she's also really nice.

03:36.140 --> 03:38.670
Every guy in the school
is drooling over her.

03:39.150 --> 03:42.310
Look at all those dropped jaws.

03:42.850 --> 03:44.650
It's so lame!

03:51.130 --> 03:52.460
I wasn't looking.

03:54.260 --> 03:55.329
You were looking.

03:55.330 --> 03:56.160
I wasn't looking.

03:56.161 --> 03:57.899
No, you were looking.

03:57.900 --> 03:59.769
Will you guys shut up?!

03:59.770 --> 04:01.260
You're making my food taste bad!

04:01.640 --> 04:06.300
But he won't admit he was staring
at Ms. Fiona with glazed eyes.

04:06.540 --> 04:09.209
What?! Ms. Fiona?!

04:09.210 --> 04:12.540
If you were staring at Ms. Fiona without
saying anything to me, I'll kill you!

04:14.080 --> 04:16.050
I told you. It's not like that.

04:16.420 --> 04:19.390
I don't want to hear it!

04:21.090 --> 04:23.759
It's all right, Osaki fox-kun.

04:23.760 --> 04:25.750
They're just playing around.

04:26.060 --> 04:28.059
Osaki fox...

04:28.060 --> 04:29.220
kun?

04:29.730 --> 04:31.130
Is that his name?

04:31.970 --> 04:33.230
Yes, it is...

04:33.430 --> 04:34.969
That's not a name.

04:34.970 --> 04:36.060
Not at all.

04:36.200 --> 04:39.309
You're not even giving him a real name?

04:39.310 --> 04:41.710
What a terrible master.

04:42.080 --> 04:42.940
Huh?

04:42.941 --> 04:45.110
In a way, it's the same as us.

04:45.750 --> 04:48.240
Fated to look after a troublesome woman.

04:49.120 --> 04:50.120
Agreed.

04:52.620 --> 04:55.419
What's your problem?!
You sure have a lot to say!

04:55.420 --> 04:59.690
So how about you give him
a name that everyone likes?!

05:00.660 --> 05:02.299
Of course!

05:02.300 --> 05:04.790
I'll give him a truly awesome name.

05:05.300 --> 05:08.290
Be in awe! Crystal Guy!

05:09.040 --> 05:09.970
Veto.

05:09.971 --> 05:11.339
Out of the question.

05:11.340 --> 05:12.639
Whose name is that?

05:12.640 --> 05:15.240
An extremely attractive
hero from a foreign drama!

05:16.640 --> 05:18.310
Then how about this?

05:20.520 --> 05:22.040
Zankuro Ozaki.

05:22.380 --> 05:23.350
It's rigid.

05:23.351 --> 05:24.480
Really rigid.

05:27.020 --> 05:28.820
I suppose it's rigid.

05:30.190 --> 05:31.660
Then I'll decide.

05:32.630 --> 05:34.120
Osaki Kitsune.

05:34.730 --> 05:36.630
A gag?

05:36.760 --> 05:37.960
It's a gag.

05:42.140 --> 05:43.400
So cold.

05:43.840 --> 05:48.040
Oh, fine! I'll give him a really cute name!

05:49.980 --> 05:51.509
I know! O-chan!

05:51.510 --> 05:53.310
It's decided: O-chan!

05:55.150 --> 05:56.719
Worst naming sense ever.

05:56.720 --> 05:57.720
Agreed.

05:57.890 --> 06:00.120
I'm definitely for Ozaki.

06:02.660 --> 06:05.130
You don't have to worry, do you, Tamaki?

06:05.230 --> 06:06.529
Huh?

06:06.530 --> 06:10.660
You're going home with
Onizaki today, too, right?

06:10.930 --> 06:12.530
The whole class is talking about it.

06:12.900 --> 06:15.300
Oh, no! There's a reason for that!

06:15.670 --> 06:17.200
And it's not just the two of us.

06:17.310 --> 06:19.039
I get it. I get it.

06:19.040 --> 06:20.579
Actually, did you know...

06:20.580 --> 06:25.379
there have been rumors among the
girls of recent disappearances in the area?

06:25.380 --> 06:26.470
Disappearances?

06:26.610 --> 06:28.819
It might just be a rumor.

06:28.820 --> 06:30.789
You can never be too careful, though.

06:30.790 --> 06:32.950
Well, you don't have to worry, Tamaki!

06:34.490 --> 06:36.790
Those two are late.

06:41.730 --> 06:42.990
What's wrong?

06:43.930 --> 06:47.560
I heard there were rumors
of disappearances in the area.

06:48.100 --> 06:53.340
Is that because the Onikirimaru's
seal is weakening like Grandma said?

06:58.610 --> 07:01.050
So that's why...

07:01.680 --> 07:03.210
Sorry to keep you waiting!

07:04.250 --> 07:05.620
Is Ohmi not here?

07:05.950 --> 07:07.110
Suguru?

07:07.360 --> 07:09.859
The gods have been restless,

07:09.860 --> 07:11.690
so he's coming just in case.

07:12.890 --> 07:14.260
Sorry I'm late.

07:18.670 --> 07:20.400
It's Ms. Fiona!

07:20.940 --> 07:22.399
Miss!

07:22.400 --> 07:25.200
I'm heading home now!

07:32.950 --> 07:35.880
Nothing beats a beautiful
woman's smile, right, Yuichi?!

07:36.250 --> 07:37.949
Is that right, Takuma?

07:37.950 --> 07:39.750
Don't ask me.

07:48.930 --> 07:52.060
Suguru, is something wrong?

07:54.370 --> 07:55.939
What are you talking about?

07:55.940 --> 07:58.130
Uh, nothing... um...

07:58.970 --> 08:02.539
That aside, have you
gotten used to this town yet?

08:02.540 --> 08:05.040
Um, yes! No...

08:05.780 --> 08:07.610
Which one is it?!

08:17.690 --> 08:20.220
It seems as though you've sensed something.

08:20.500 --> 08:23.690
The gods are probably
restless deep in the woods.

08:24.370 --> 08:28.170
Is that because the
Onikirimaru's seal has weakened?

08:32.310 --> 08:35.830
What exactly is the Onikirimaru seal?

08:42.050 --> 08:46.710
The Onikirimaru seal is
protected by two other seals.

08:47.320 --> 08:49.259
The first is the blood of the Tamayori.

08:49.260 --> 08:53.090
The second is the five
seals known as the Artifacts.

08:53.830 --> 08:59.630
The five Artifacts are kept in
locations known as Seal Grounds.

09:01.340 --> 09:05.409
The previous era's Tamayori
princess, Lady Baba,

09:05.410 --> 09:08.000
and our ancestors, have
protected the Artifacts.

09:09.240 --> 09:13.209
As to why it has been weakening recently,

09:13.210 --> 09:15.519
we, the protectors, do not know.

09:15.520 --> 09:16.780
You don't know?

09:17.180 --> 09:19.180
We have the duty to protect.

09:20.190 --> 09:24.320
Aside from the necessary,
we are not told anything.

09:25.530 --> 09:28.390
We are nothing more than tools, after all.

09:29.160 --> 09:31.199
Tools do not think.

09:31.200 --> 09:34.899
Not about why we exist, where we come from,

09:34.900 --> 09:36.560
nor where we are going.

09:38.070 --> 09:40.170
<i>Saying things like that again...</i>

09:41.640 --> 09:43.040
I want to know!

09:43.410 --> 09:45.779
Being told I'm the one who
carries the Tamayori's blood,

09:45.780 --> 09:48.250
or that I must protect the Onikirimaru,

09:48.780 --> 09:51.750
doesn't tell me what I should do.

09:52.390 --> 09:55.320
I want to learn more about
the Tamayori princess!

09:56.560 --> 09:59.059
More? Like what?

09:59.060 --> 10:00.529
Anything.

10:00.530 --> 10:03.360
What the Tamayori princess
has done, or the history.

10:07.840 --> 10:09.099
What's wrong?

10:09.100 --> 10:11.230
All the information is at
your warehouse, right?

10:13.310 --> 10:15.040
It wouldn't be anywhere else.

10:16.310 --> 10:17.470
Yeah.

10:20.880 --> 10:22.010
Let's go.

10:22.880 --> 10:24.110
Yes!

10:30.160 --> 10:31.829
This one doesn't work either.

10:31.830 --> 10:33.560
It should be one of these.

10:34.460 --> 10:35.490
Move!

10:42.770 --> 10:44.530
It's no use. It won't even budge.

10:44.840 --> 10:46.709
There is no door that cannot be opened.

10:46.710 --> 10:48.570
I believe so, too.

10:48.810 --> 10:52.140
There may be some kind of trick.

10:52.680 --> 10:55.480
Hey, you, the spaced out one.

10:56.450 --> 10:58.649
Place your hand on the door and say,

10:58.650 --> 11:00.319
"Thy master here comes."

11:00.320 --> 11:02.289
Thy master here comes?

11:02.290 --> 11:03.450
Yes, just do it!

11:04.130 --> 11:05.150
Fine!

11:06.360 --> 11:08.960
Thy master here comes.

11:13.830 --> 11:16.300
Nothing's happening, is-

11:29.120 --> 11:31.550
Wh-Why?

11:33.390 --> 11:36.389
The Tamayori princess blood
barrier was placed upon it.

11:36.390 --> 11:38.620
Mahiro, how do you know that?

11:38.890 --> 11:40.450
What does it matter?

11:55.110 --> 11:56.940
A-Amazing...

11:58.110 --> 12:00.450
But it smells a little moldy.

12:08.690 --> 12:10.210
The portal...

12:12.930 --> 12:14.099
Are you okay?

12:14.100 --> 12:15.190
You're pale.

12:15.930 --> 12:16.700
Yes.

12:16.701 --> 12:20.460
For the moment, it may be best to leave.

12:24.410 --> 12:26.269
<i>That voice...</i>

12:26.270 --> 12:28.370
<i>was the same as the voice
I heard in my dream.</i>

12:29.780 --> 12:32.080
Well? Are you feeling better?

12:32.910 --> 12:35.410
Yes, thank you.

12:35.780 --> 12:38.510
Seriously. You get
anemic at the drop of a hat.

12:38.890 --> 12:41.389
How are we supposed to do any research?

12:41.390 --> 12:42.459
I know...

12:42.460 --> 12:46.690
Tamaki, you are undoubtedly
the Tamayori princess.

12:47.430 --> 12:48.859
How do you know?

12:48.860 --> 12:52.869
You broke the Tamayori barrier
that was placed on the warehouse,

12:52.870 --> 12:57.669
and the moment you stepped
inside and touched something,

12:57.670 --> 13:01.940
it responded and powerful
thoughts flowed toward you.

13:02.980 --> 13:04.410
Am I wrong?

13:06.110 --> 13:09.210
That was because you
are the Tamayori princess.

13:11.990 --> 13:15.950
But I still don't know what to do.

13:16.090 --> 13:19.220
That's why we're helping, isn't it?

13:20.430 --> 13:22.259
We're here to protect
the Tamayori princess,

13:22.260 --> 13:24.290
and that means you.

13:24.970 --> 13:26.769
You don't have to worry about anything.

13:26.770 --> 13:29.669
Well, with an unreliable
Tamayori princess like you,

13:29.670 --> 13:31.760
what choice do we have?

13:33.510 --> 13:34.910
You guys...

13:36.410 --> 13:38.479
If you try to look too far ahead,

13:38.480 --> 13:40.450
you won't be able to
see where you're walking.

13:41.080 --> 13:42.810
Let's leave it at this for today.

13:43.380 --> 13:44.410
Okay.

13:50.190 --> 13:51.660
So that's it?

13:52.730 --> 13:53.990
Yes.

14:00.370 --> 14:02.770
Another barrier here?

14:07.210 --> 14:09.770
We're out of time.

14:13.810 --> 14:15.080
Mitsuru.

14:15.550 --> 14:16.640
Yes?

14:23.160 --> 14:25.320
May I ask a favor of you?

14:35.070 --> 14:37.200
A problem with the seal?

14:37.340 --> 14:39.810
Yes, I heard from Ohmi this morning.

14:40.040 --> 14:44.380
There was a report of strange movements
at the location of the first Artifact.

14:45.110 --> 14:47.050
I'm going to investigate on my way home.

14:47.350 --> 14:50.050
It sounds like there's more to it.

14:51.590 --> 14:53.889
Actually, three months ago,

14:53.890 --> 14:57.289
although only for a brief moment,

14:57.290 --> 14:59.230
the seal apparently vanished.

14:59.530 --> 15:00.550
What did you say?

15:00.690 --> 15:02.530
I hadn't heard about this!

15:03.400 --> 15:05.530
They thought it was an
unpredictable accident.

15:06.130 --> 15:10.499
But the fact that there were strange
movements at an Artifact location

15:10.500 --> 15:14.239
at the same time the
Onikirimaru seal weakened...

15:14.240 --> 15:16.340
seems like more than a coincidence.

15:16.780 --> 15:18.979
So Lady Baba noticed this,

15:18.980 --> 15:20.979
and called him here.

15:20.980 --> 15:22.310
Seems like it.

15:24.250 --> 15:27.789
All right. Then after we
take her home from school,

15:27.790 --> 15:29.220
we'll check out the seal location.

15:30.720 --> 15:32.159
I'm going, too.

15:32.160 --> 15:33.289
I want to go!

15:33.290 --> 15:34.459
You want to go?

15:34.460 --> 15:35.759
Do you even know what you're saying?

15:35.760 --> 15:39.629
Yes. I know that even if I go,
I won't be able to do anything,

15:39.630 --> 15:41.769
but I want to see the seal location.

15:41.770 --> 15:43.169
You want to see it?

15:43.170 --> 15:44.900
It isn't a tourist attraction.

15:45.140 --> 15:46.230
Wait.

15:47.240 --> 15:49.379
She may slow us down,

15:49.380 --> 15:51.409
but as long as we're
there, she should be fine.

15:51.410 --> 15:52.449
That's right.

15:52.450 --> 15:54.610
We can protect a single princess.

15:56.920 --> 15:58.480
Do as you please.

16:03.590 --> 16:04.590
Ohmi!

16:07.160 --> 16:09.150
The princess says she
wants to see the seal, too.

16:11.200 --> 16:12.769
Understood.

16:12.770 --> 16:17.099
This way. Beyond here
is the Tamayori barrier.

16:17.100 --> 16:18.400
The land of the gods.

16:26.950 --> 16:29.080
This is the barrier?

16:45.330 --> 16:48.539
This is the first Seal Ground.

16:48.540 --> 16:50.500
There doesn't appear
to be anything different.

16:50.970 --> 16:52.409
Okay.

16:52.410 --> 16:54.770
Okay! Let's go to the next one!

17:05.890 --> 17:07.119
Huh?

17:07.120 --> 17:09.420
I thought I sensed someone...

17:09.820 --> 17:10.820
Offering.

17:12.160 --> 17:14.190
Offering. Offering.

17:14.900 --> 17:16.859
Offering. Offering.

17:16.860 --> 17:18.630
Offering. Offering.

17:19.530 --> 17:21.020
You're the thing from...

17:21.240 --> 17:24.039
Oh, I get it! An offering, right?

17:24.040 --> 17:25.970
Let's see...

17:28.210 --> 17:29.610
There it is!

17:31.680 --> 17:32.980
Here, an offering.

17:39.850 --> 17:42.190
S-So many...

17:42.920 --> 17:44.860
Hey, what are you doing?

17:45.490 --> 17:47.530
If you keep messing around,
we'll leave you behind.

17:48.030 --> 17:49.050
Okay!

17:49.200 --> 17:51.530
I'm sorry. I only have one.

17:51.770 --> 17:53.630
Well, see you!

18:01.940 --> 18:04.240
I'd felt something for a while now.

18:04.550 --> 18:05.679
So it was drowned gods!

18:05.680 --> 18:07.249
This could be troublesome.

18:07.250 --> 18:08.779
Does someone have the
amulet of incantations?

18:08.780 --> 18:11.270
I don't always
conveniently carry it around!

18:13.850 --> 18:15.059
Stay back!

18:15.060 --> 18:16.750
We have no desire to fight you.

18:20.560 --> 18:22.120
That won't work. They're frenzied!

18:23.130 --> 18:24.360
Let's get them!

18:28.600 --> 18:29.870
Gittora!

18:31.940 --> 18:32.940
Go!

18:35.210 --> 18:36.340
Genshutsu!

18:39.650 --> 18:41.010
Amazing...

18:47.720 --> 18:49.690
What's with these numbers?

18:49.760 --> 18:50.789
Indeed.

18:50.790 --> 18:53.260
This seems like more than
just a weakening of the seal.

18:53.630 --> 18:57.290
Tamaki, retreat within
the Seal Ground barrier.

18:58.970 --> 19:01.139
You'll be safe there.

19:01.140 --> 19:03.160
Go while we hold them off!

19:03.440 --> 19:05.170
That's... But...

19:07.140 --> 19:08.800
Just go already!

19:20.950 --> 19:22.919
I want to eat!

19:22.920 --> 19:24.629
I want to eat!

19:24.630 --> 19:25.920
I want to eat!

19:29.560 --> 19:30.530
Now!

19:30.530 --> 19:31.530
Hurry!

19:31.570 --> 19:32.570
Okay!

19:32.571 --> 19:33.970
Thank you, O-chan!

19:38.840 --> 19:39.900
O-chan!

19:40.110 --> 19:41.639
Don't get in my way!

19:41.640 --> 19:42.940
Don't!

19:46.650 --> 19:49.279
The Tamayori's blood.

19:49.280 --> 19:50.819
Looks delicious.

19:50.820 --> 19:52.510
I want to eat!

20:02.460 --> 20:05.090
Go back to the underworld!

20:33.760 --> 20:35.099
I see.

20:35.100 --> 20:39.830
So that's the power of the Shugogo house.

20:44.240 --> 20:46.140
It's all right now.

20:46.740 --> 20:48.179
Are you injured?

20:48.180 --> 20:49.830
N-No-

20:48.780 --> 20:49.830
Why?

20:50.640 --> 20:52.040
Why did you come back?

20:52.510 --> 20:55.040
If you die, then we
have no reason to fight!

20:55.920 --> 20:57.619
I'm sorry.

20:57.620 --> 20:58.790
But-

20:57.880 --> 20:59.750
Hell, it's okay, isn't it?

21:00.390 --> 21:03.450
The desire to help a
companion isn't a bad thing.

21:04.420 --> 21:05.330
Agreed.

21:05.331 --> 21:06.371
I don't dislike it either.

21:07.590 --> 21:08.930
That's right.

21:17.670 --> 21:19.610
Thank you, everyone.

21:20.810 --> 21:22.079
Really?

21:22.080 --> 21:25.270
So her powers didn't appear today either.

21:26.110 --> 21:27.210
Yes.

21:27.650 --> 21:32.619
But she must do something herself,

21:32.620 --> 21:36.319
before her time comes to
perform the Onikirimaru seal's ritual.

21:36.320 --> 21:39.420
I hope she makes it in time.

21:40.960 --> 21:42.220
Yes.

21:43.360 --> 21:47.399
From between the trees

21:47.400 --> 21:55.309
The evening sun spills
onto this tree lined street

21:55.310 --> 22:00.809
Talking and laughing

22:00.810 --> 22:06.220
Mysteriously made me feel at ease

22:08.690 --> 22:15.029
Since the two of us met that day

22:15.030 --> 22:18.899
Through the time we have spent together

22:18.900 --> 22:26.900
This feeling has grown

22:32.380 --> 22:35.119
In order to protect you

22:35.120 --> 22:40.689
I am here right now

22:40.690 --> 22:46.559
You try to act strong

22:46.560 --> 22:51.329
But I will accept all your weaknesses

22:51.330 --> 22:54.169
No matter how small

22:54.170 --> 22:59.569
You can rely on me for anything

22:59.570 --> 23:06.880
If you trip I will catch
you with these hands

23:16.960 --> 23:17.960
Stop!

23:26.530 --> 23:29.730
Um, are you all right?

23:36.980 --> 23:40.040
Today was fun.

23:44.120 --> 23:45.550
Let's meet again.

23:48.960 --> 23:52.890
I'll always be here waiting.

23:54.260 --> 24:01.030
Next time: The Five Guardians
